<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Block-Level Elements Demo</title>
    <style>
        .section-container {
            border: 3px solid #2c3e50;
            margin: 20px;
            padding: 15px;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
        }

        .button-section {
            border: 3px dashed #e74c3c;
            margin: 20px;
            padding: 15px;
            background-color: #fdf2f2;
        }

        h1, p, div {
            border: 1px solid #3498db;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        img {
            display: block;
            max-width: 200px;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }

        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="section-container">
        <h1>Heading (Block Element)</h1>
        <p>This paragraph is a block-level element. Notice how the blue borders show that these elements extend the full width of their container.</p>
        <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/200" alt="Placeholder Image">
    </div>

    <div class="button-section">
        <button type="button">Action Button</button>
    </div>

</body>
</html>